    "description": "Corrected oracle rolled forward by the 2026-10 hunger corrections (docs/integration/hunger-mortality.md). Captured with the exact capture loops of tests/test_performance_equivalence.py and tests/test_governance_dormancy.py in Python off mode with the native ecology/politics runtimes disabled. Each workload index is the first turn that correction moves relative to the oracle with all earlier corrections applied (consecutive captures). corrected_food_logistics_2026_10 and older fixtures remain frozen; workloads not named in 'corrections' are byte-identical to it.",
    "corrections": [
      {
        "id": "HM-DEARTH-WEIGHT",
        "summary": "A dearth report drains a third of a famine's stability, and its five-turn cooldown weighs a third of a famine's in hazard hardship, civ stress, technique growth and nomad raid hunger.",
        "workloads": {},
        "note": "Dearth labels exist only in agent modes; an aggregate famine keeps the full weight."
      },
      {
        "id": "HM-EPIDEMIC-HUNGER",
        "summary": "Agent modes: epidemic susceptibility (+0.15 dearth, +0.35 famine) and fatality (x1 + 0.10 dearth + 0.40 famine) follow the region's last measured hunger instead of a report's cooldown.",
        "workloads": {},
        "note": "The aggregate model keeps the flat famine terms; the oracle lane also runs with epidemiology off."
      },
      {
        "id": "HM-NATIVE-DEMOGRAPHY",
        "summary": "Native agent mortality gains a hunger hazard for young children, the old and the poor, and fertility a hunger multiplier, from food sufficiency and the severe-shortage run (region batch column food_severe_turns).",
        "workloads": {},
        "note": "Native agent runtime only."
      },
      {
        "id": "HM-AGGREGATE-TOLL",
        "summary": "The aggregate famine toll (5 x stress multiplier, a famine's whole population effect in the aggregate model) is scaled by the report's hunger: the share of a total, sustained famine's added mortality carried by the depth of the food yield below the famine threshold (0.12).",
        "workloads": {
          "standard": 0,
          "wide": 9
        }
      }
    ],
    "environment": {
      "python": "3.13.17",
      "platform": "Linux"
    },
    "comparison": "complete emitted file set, byte count and SHA256; no field filtering or tolerance",
    "projections": "workloads: bundle version 5 bytes (scripts/third_wave_controls.py projection); pre_pruning_workloads: the same run projected to bundle version 4 (legacy_artifact_bytes(pre_pruning=True))."
